# MQ04 "Weynon Priory". MQ03 50 set 60, which starts MQ04 at 5: the Mythic Dawn attack the Priory and Prior Maborel
# lies dead. Near the Priory Eronor runs to the player (7) and says Jauffre is in the Chapel (10, which ends MQ03 at
# 100). Jauffre fights in the Chapel; he goes with the player to check on the Amulet (20), the chest in Weynon House
# is empty (25), and he names Cloud Ruler Temple (30). At its gates (35) the Blades hail Martin (36 .. 44), the
# quest waits (45), and "And you will be the Emperor." to Martin sets 50 -> 100, which starts MQ05 at 10.
# DRAFT from tools/live/quest_brief.py (2026-11-12): not run yet.

# The ride from Kvatch is the player's travel: `cow` stands in for it and Martin, who follows the player, is brought
# along. EronorScript sets 7 once the player is within 5000 of him; his find-the-player package ends at the player
# and his greeting ("Help! You must help! ...") offers "Hold on. Tell me what happened." (INFO 0001EE29) -> "Who's
# attacking Weynon Priory?" (INFO 0001EE28) -> "Where's Jauffre? Is he safe?" (INFO 0001EE2A, 10; run 23a: only
# the first is listed at the greeting). The agents attack on sight: the
# player fights (`defend`), and keeps Martin alive. Stage 7 also sends agents 03 and 05 at the player, and
# Skyrim's dialogue does not pause the game as Oblivion's does: an attack while Eronor greets closes his
# conversation, his package changes and EronorScript sets 10 without the topics (run 39c). The player deals with
# those two as they arrive (the kill stands in for the fight). Stage 7 also sends agent 04 at Brother Piner; his
# death during the greeting alarmed Eronor the same way (run 57b), so the player stops agent 04 too. (Agent 01 is
# the leader fighting Jauffre in the Chapel, the next case's fight.)
case mq04_arrive_priory
until 600 GetStage MQ04 >= 5
defend MartinRef
run
MQ04MythicDawnAgent03Ref.kill
MQ04MythicDawnAgent04Ref.kill
MQ04MythicDawnAgent05Ref.kill
cow TES4Tamriel -14 21
wait 120
run
MartinRef.moveto player
until 900 GetStage MQ04 >= 7
approach EronorRef
talk EronorRef
ask "Hold on. Tell me what happened."
ask "Who's attacking Weynon Priory?"
ask "Where's Jauffre? Is he safe?"
until 300 GetStage MQ04 >= 10
until 300 GetStageDone MQ03 100
bye if open
end

# Jauffre is in the Chapel (WeynonPrioryChapel), fighting; the player helps him. "I'll go check on the Amulet."
# (INFO 0001EE2B, MQ04.playerFoundSecretRoom == 0) sets 20. MQ04 makes Jauffre mortal for the fight, and his death
# at stages 10..19 is Oblivion's game over (JauffreScript OnDeath: EssentialDeathReload); at test pace agent 01 killed him within a
# second of the Chapel loading, before `defend` acted (run 58d), so the player strikes the two agents as they arrive.
case mq04_find_jauffre
defend JauffreRef
run
player.moveto JauffreRef
MQ04MythicDawnAgent01Ref.kill
MQ04MythicDawnAgent02Ref.kill
wait 120
approach JauffreRef
talk JauffreRef
ask "I'll go check on the Amulet."
until 300 GetStage MQ04 >= 20
bye if open
end

# The Amulet's chest in Weynon House (MQ04AmuletChestRef, behind the secret door stage 5 opened) is empty: opening
# it at 20 sets 25 (MQ04AmuletChestScript). Jauffre comes along (27 = his walk to MQ04JauffreAmuletMarker ends).
# At 27 he has seen it himself: his greeting "They've taken it! The Amulet of Kings is gone!" (INFO 00090B4F)
# offers "I found Martin. He is safe." (INFO 0001EE2D), which offers "Where will Martin be safe?" (INFO 0001EE2E,
# 30). ("The Amulet is gone." belongs to his greetings before 27; run 23b.) The player opens the chest as soon as
# they land: Jauffre reaching it sets 27 by himself (OnPackageDone MQ04JauffreToAmulet), and a chest opened in the
# middle of his greeting cut off its choice (run 39d, after a fixed `wait 120`; again at once in 39e, when he was
# 70 ticks away). When his 27 force greet (MQ04JauffreGreetPlayer) is already open with its choice, the player
# answers it there: since the exit hold, Goodbye is locked while a choice is offered (as in Oblivion). Otherwise
# the player walks up and talks; the 27 greeting is not say-once and offers its choice again.
case mq04_amulet_gone
defend JauffreRef
run
player.moveto MQ04AmuletChestRef
until 300 player.GetDistance MQ04AmuletChestRef < 300
activate MQ04AmuletChestRef
until 300 GetStage MQ04 >= 25
close ContainerMenu
until 1800 GetStage MQ04 >= 27
approach JauffreRef
talk JauffreRef
ask "I found Martin. He is safe."
ask "Where will Martin be safe?"
until 300 GetStage MQ04 >= 30
bye if open
end

# The ride to Cloud Ruler Temple is the player's travel with Martin and Jauffre: all three are placed at the gates.
# MQ04Script sets 35 once Martin is within 1000 and Jauffre within 1250 of CloudRulerMainGates; Jauffre's "Come.
# Your Blades are waiting to greet you." sets 36, the script 40, Jauffre reaching the steps 41, and the Blades'
# hail runs 42 .. 44; the script then sets 45.
case mq04_cloud_ruler
run
player.moveto MQ04MartinOutsideCloudRulerMarker
wait 120
run
MartinRef.moveto MQ04MartinOutsideCloudRulerMarker
JauffreRef.moveto MQ04JauffreOutsideCloudRulerMarker
until 1800 GetStage MQ04 >= 35
until 1800 GetStage MQ04 >= 36
until 1800 GetStage MQ04 >= 40
until 3600 GetStage MQ04 >= 41
until 3600 GetStage MQ04 >= 44
until 1800 GetStage MQ04 >= 45
end

# Martin, inside the Temple: his greeting at 44 .. 45 (INFO 0001EFE0) offers "We need to get the Amulet back."
# (INFO 0001EFE1), which offers "And you will be the Emperor." (INFO 0001EFE2): that sets 50, whose result sets
# 100; that ends MQ04 and sets MQ05 10. (Run 24a: only the first is listed at the greeting.)
case mq04_martin_emperor
run
player.moveto MartinRef
wait 120
approach MartinRef
talk MartinRef
ask "We need to get the Amulet back."
ask "And you will be the Emperor."
until 300 GetStage MQ04 >= 50
until 300 GetStageDone MQ04 100
until 300 GetStage MQ05 >= 10
bye if open
end
